From 35c0b86b7cd7e78828d7248841ef1264c0a53d04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:49:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] range: getClientRects/getBoundingClientRect return the
 selected text's glyph boxes

Range.getClientRects() walked start.following_nodes() up to the end node, which
skipped the start node, ran to the end of the document when start and end were
the same node, and returned whole-node border boxes (text nodes have none, so
the result was mostly unrelated elements). getBoundingClientRect() then folded
those from a zero rect at the origin. Tooltips, popovers and Wikipedia
reference previews anchored to ranges were placed far from their text.

Follow CSSOM View instead: visit the nodes from the start node to the end
boundary point, include the border boxes of contained elements whose parent is
not contained, and for each selected or partially selected Text node include
the boxes of just its selected characters, one per line box. The bounding rect
skips empty rects and falls back to the first one.

The text boxes come from a new layout query. Text fragments now record the
index of their first character in the inline formatting context, and text runs
record which characters each DOM text node produced (several adjacent nodes can
share a run), along with the white space and capitalization state needed to
replay the node's text transformation so DOM UTF-16 offsets can be mapped to
rendered characters. The box block size is ascent plus descent, as in Chrome.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
